low-licm: loop-invariant code motion for descriptor-backed low CFGs, after low-cse in packetization preparation, plus a
second low-cse. Inert unless LOOM_EXP_LICM=1 (the pipeline schedules it only then), so default output is unchanged; the
engine sets it per kernel (emit_prefill_pp: the fp16 and kv4-QROT prefill attention). Only pure ALU packets move (no
memory, matrix, control, state writes, tied or effect rows; operands defined outside the loop; loops with a dedicated
preheader; no new blocks). The fragment loads' per-lane LDS address math, re-derived every tile, leaves the attention
loop: fp16 attention -1.0% (pp2048) / -2.15% (32K context), kv4 QROT -0.5% (LOOM_EXP_LICM_MAX_LIVE=1), bit-identical;
the afrag GEMMs lose 5-20% (register pressure), so they keep it off. Knobs: LOOM_EXP_LICM_MAX (packets),
LOOM_EXP_LICM_MAX_LIVE (new loop-live units), LOOM_EXP_LICM_SALU, LOOM_EXP_LICM_DEBUG.

